Z||000001||sjp777||06-21-2001||09:14 PM||||If the speedo works and the od doesn't, it's got to be the little motor or its connection on the gauge. The motor that drives the od is seperate from the speedo motor. You have to pull the gauge pod apart to get at it.<P>for those tired of watching their mileage rise. The od can be disabled by unplugging the od motor from the circuit board that makes up the back of the speedo.<P>The speedo will still work as well as the trip od.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||06-22-2001||11:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sjp777:<BR><B>For those tired of watching their mileage rise. The od can be disabled by unplugging the od motor from the circuit board that makes up the back of the speedo.<P>The speedo will still work as well as the trip od.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>&gt;Or if you have my car, you can watch the miles going backward.  If does catch up though.<P>||||reg||1
